request.description:
Response:
```
{
  id, email, firstName, lastName, role, netsuiteInternalId, mustChangePassword, lastLoginAt,
  employee: {
    jobTitle, departmentName, subsidiaryName, currencyCode,
    developer: boolean, salesRep: boolean, productDeveloper: boolean
  } | null
}
```
`employee` is `null` when the user isn't linked to a NetSuite employee record (e.g. an admin-created account, or a test account with no real employee data). Use this for a Profile/Account page — it's the richest identity endpoint.
